<title>UK: BES Overseas Ltd sets $200 mln perpetual FRN, call.</title>
<headline>BES Overseas Ltd sets $200 mln perpetual FRN, call.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by joint lead managers Merrill Lynch, Banco Espirito Santo and Banco ESSI S.A..</p>
<p> BORROWER   BES OVERSEAS LTD</p>
<p>GUARANTOR**BANCO ESPIRITO SANTO AND COMERCIAL DE LISBOA SA</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	SPREAD     +195 BP   MATURITY   *PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE    ***FRN	 BASE	 3M LIBOR  PAY DATE    15.NOV.96</p>
<p> EXP MOODY BAA1	 ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   3.15 PCT</p>
<p> EXP S&amp;P   BBB	  REOFFER    PAR</p>
<p> NOTES	*CALL OPTION IN FIFTH YEAR AND QUARTERLY THEREAFTER</p>
<p>		NO PUT OPTIONS</p>
<p>		**ON A SUBORDINATED BASIS</p>
<p>		***NON-CUMULATED PERPETUAL PREFERRED FLOATING RATE</p>
<p>		SECURITIES</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS     25	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/PT</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
